// AUTO-GENERATED — do not hand-edit. The header/footer bands for every branded
// download template, base64-encoded so they are reliably available to the
// serverless download routes (reading public/ via fs is not guaranteed on Vercel
// — same rationale as src/lib/letterhead-logo.ts).
//
// Each band is a single full-width JPEG strip that already contains BOTH logos
// (brand + partner) plus the surrounding text and rules, so every template is
// pixel-faithful to the client's own artwork. The _W/_H values are the pixel dims
// of the strip, used to size it proportionally to the page content width.
//
// PROVENANCE — every band is the client's own letterhead image, lifted out of
// the file they supplied. Nothing here is a rebuild or a re-render:
//
//   TRC_*  — from word/media/ inside the five "Template TRC - *.docx", where the
//            letterhead already IS a single band image (2126x257 header /
//            2126x287 footer). Downscaled to 1400px wide (~208dpi at A4 content
//            width) and re-encoded at q0.95; the artwork itself is untouched.
//            All five share one geometry because the source files do.
//
//   GFDI_* — no .docx was supplied for these, only PDFs — but those PDFs still
//            carry the bands as embedded DCTDecode (JPEG) image XObjects, so they
//            were extracted BYTE-FOR-BYTE out of the PDF streams rather than
//            rasterised. Sizes differ per publication (1339-1358px wide) because
//            that is how the client's artwork was authored.
//
// HOW TO ADD A NINTH TEMPLATE — in preference order, because it matters:
//   1. .docx supplied?  unzip it and take word/media/ (what TRC_* did).
//   2. PDF supplied?    scan for /Subtype /Image with /Filter /DCTDecode and copy
//                       the stream out (what GFDI_* did). Check the extracted
//                       image is the WHOLE band — logos AND surrounding text —
//                       and not just one logo placed next to vector text.
//   3. Neither works?   only then rasterise the page and crop to the sample's own
//                       content column, and use ONE x range for both bands or the
//                       logo and the footer rule land on different margins.
// Then add the three constants here plus the registry.ts entry and its BandKey.

